{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd6edffc4dee485e20e41856","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":{"value":"pm-u9d0","source":"argv"},"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-6xlyss"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Absence-tolerant readers accept only ENOENT, so a tracker root that is a regular file raises an unclassified fault instead of the typed refusal the guard already owns — and that fault blocks the daily release"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","area:sdk","defect-recurrence","error-taxonomy","gate","refusal-typing","release-blocker"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"readWorkspaceContextIntentContracts treats ENOTDIR as absence so the authoritative tracker-root guard emits the refusal; A shared isFileAbsentError helper expresses the ENOENT/ENOTDIR equivalence in one place; A ratchet gate fails any NEW catch clause that tolerates ENOENT without ENOTDIR; The remaining 45 declared sites are reviewed per-site and the ceiling reaches 0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm-cli 2026.8.9, node v26.5.0, linux; observed in production telemetry and reproduced locally"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"1. touch ./notadir  2. pm list --path ./notadir"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A typed usage/not-found refusal (PmCliError), which shouldCaptureCliError excludes from Sentry."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Raw Node ENOTDIR escapes as unclassified_runtime_error, is captured to Sentry as PM-CLI-2X 'Error: ENOTDIR: not a directory, open', classified unexpected_fault, and fails sentry-telemetry-gate (max_high 0) — blocking every daily Auto Release cut."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"sdk/context-intent-runtime, core/fs/fs-utils, release/sentry-telemetry-gate"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7rrqsk","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-h75tjh","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-qxo5iu","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-w7ccmv","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xp1xsw","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-10T05:50:32.166Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b42e57b364c46ec19bd477bd80e35c8b0ec386f5aaaa025d6221984b00f558f6","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:51:29.541Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd6edffc4dee485e20e41856","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":{"value":"pm-6xlyss","source":"argv"},"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:51:29.541Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:51:29.524Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"probe"}]}],"before_hash":"b42e57b364c46ec19bd477bd80e35c8b0ec386f5aaaa025d6221984b00f558f6","after_hash":"d79314bbe1da3bf5a744007acec3a5ae85806a67a77a44b1fe0b30f826eb5330"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:52:04.892Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd6edffc4dee485e20e41856","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":{"value":"pm-6xlyss","source":"argv"},"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## What the record shows\n\nThe daily scheduled Auto Release run failed on `sentry-telemetry-gate` with `max_high: 0` and one blocking issue:\n\n```\n\"blocking_short_ids\": [\"PM-CLI-2X\"],\n\"blocking_titles\": [\"Error: ENOTDIR: not a directory, open\"],\n\"blocking_reasons\": [{\"short_id\": \"PM-CLI-2X\", \"reason\": \"unexpected_fault\"}]\n```\n\nThe gate is correct. The event is a genuine unclassified fault. The defect is that it should never have been a fault at all.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`readWorkspaceContextIntentContracts` reads the optional `context-intents.json` and tolerates only `ENOENT`:\n\n```ts\nif (isRecord(error) && typeof error.code === \"string\" && error.code === \"ENOENT\") return [];\nthrow error;\n```\n\nWhen the tracker root is a regular file, Node reports `ENOTDIR`, not `ENOENT`. For an **optional** read those two errno values answer the same question - the file is not there and cannot be there - but only one of them is accepted, so the raw error escapes.\n\nThe guard that owns this refusal already exists and is correct. `assertItemMetadataRoot` in `core/store/item-store.ts` raises a typed `tracker_root_not_directory` usage refusal for exactly this state. It simply never runs: the optional declaration read happens **earlier in the command pipeline** and throws first.\n\nThis is the recurrence family owned by pm-7rrqsk - a newer read path added without picking up an established guard. The consequence chain is what makes it expensive:\n\nuntyped fault -> `shouldCaptureCliError` returns true -> Sentry `unexpected_fault` -> release gate `max_high` breached -> every daily cut blocked.\n\n## Population\n\nAn AST scan of `src/**/*.ts` for catch clauses that name `ENOENT` without `ENOTDIR` found **45** sites after the two central fixes. Most are not reachable from a misdirected root today, but each is the same latent shape, and any one of them can become the next release blocker the same way this one did.\n\n## Disposition\n\nShipped in this change:\n\n- `isFileAbsentError` in `core/fs/fs-utils.ts` states the equivalence once; `readFileIfExists` and `removeFileIfExists` adopt it.\n- `sdk/context-intent-runtime.ts` uses it, so the authoritative root guard now speaks instead of the optional reader.\n- `scripts/release/absence-tolerance-gate.mjs` ratchets the population. The bound fails in **both** directions: a higher count is a regression, a lower one is an undeclared improvement that must be written down so the next regression cannot hide beneath slack.\n\nLeft open by this item: driving the declared ceiling from 45 to 0 by reviewing each remaining site, since a blind rewrite would wrongly silence readers where `ENOTDIR` really does mean corruption rather than absence.\n\n## Verification\n\n`pm list --path <a regular file>` now exits 3 with a typed refusal and is not captured to Sentry."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:52:04.892Z"}],"before_hash":"d79314bbe1da3bf5a744007acec3a5ae85806a67a77a44b1fe0b30f826eb5330","after_hash":"92df8d675e189e6379f81709e7a54ab9e91a523be0a31e16df499efa71107097"}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T05:52:24.884Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dd6edffc4dee485e20e41856","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":{"value":"pm-6xlyss","source":"argv"},"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"The gate that blocked the release was right; the event it blocked on was the bug. Asking 'could this fault have been a refusal?' is the cheaper question than asking 'is this gate too strict?'."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-10T05:52:24.884Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"An authoritative guard is only as good as its position in the pipeline. tracker_root_not_directory was correct, tested, and unreachable, because a later-added optional read ran before it. Ordering, not absence, was the defect."},{"created_at":"2026-08-10T05:52:24.862Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"For an optional read, ENOENT and ENOTDIR are the same answer reached from different directions. Any absence-tolerant reader that accepts only ENOENT converts a graceful default into an unclassified fault the moment a path component is a regular file - and an untyped fault is the one thing the release gate cannot forgive."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"src/core/fs/fs-utils.ts","scope":"project"},{"path":"src/sdk/context-intent-runtime.ts","scope":"project"},{"path":"scripts/release/absence-tolerance-gate.mjs","scope":"project"},{"path":"scripts/release/absence-tolerance-baseline.json","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"npx vitest run tests/unit/scripts/release/absence-tolerance-gate.spec.ts","path":"tests/unit/scripts/release/absence-tolerance-gate.spec.ts","scope":"project"},{"command":"npx vitest run tests/unit/core/fs/fs-utils.spec.ts","path":"tests/unit/core/fs/fs-utils.spec.ts","scope":"project"}]}],"before_hash":"92df8d675e189e6379f81709e7a54ab9e91a523be0a31e16df499efa71107097","after_hash":"afc54e25d2f092c7c925ef4fc2787d7e9602354054996e9bae710d2c1501994b"}
